    "text": "<p>A hall has a square floor of dimension <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> (see the figure) and vertical walls. If the angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>H</mi></math> between the diagonals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>G</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>H</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the height of the hall (in meters) is:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0136_2f48b5843516.png\" style=\"width: 272px; height: 268px;\" /></p>"
